    "raw": "Given:\n- Wanda brings 90 pieces of bread.\n- Wanda brings three times as many pieces of bread as treats.\n- Wanda brings half as many treats as Jane.\n- Jane brings 75% as many pieces of bread as treats.\n\nFirst, let's find out how many treats Wanda brings. Since Wanda brings three times as many pieces of bread as treats, and she brings 90 pieces of bread, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ \\text{Number of treats Wanda brings} = \\frac{90}{3} = 30 \\]\n\nNext, we know Wanda brings half as many treats as Jane, so:\n\\[ \\text{Number of treats Jane brings} = 30 \\times 2 = 60 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find out how many pieces of bread Jane brings. Since Jane brings 75% as many pieces of bread as treats, and she brings 60 treats, we can calculate:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pieces of bread Jane brings} = 60 \\times 0.75 = 45 \\]\n\nNow, we can find the total number of pieces of bread and treats that Wanda and Jane brought to the zoo:\n\\[ \\text{Total pieces of bread} = 90 + 45 = 135 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total treats} = 30 + 60 = 90 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total number of pieces of bread and treats} = 135 + 90 = 225 \\]\n\nFINAL: 225",
